  "restoration_note": "Teaching 40 unfolds as a tight mechanical sequence: Sin builds a body from the five Worlds of Darkness, binds the soul's five faculties (mind/thought/teaching/counsel/reflection) into five somatic substrates (bone/sinew/vein/flesh/skin), and overlays Sin's counter-faculties as exousiastai. The Mind of Light then performs an exact inverse exchange — raising each soul-faculty out, binding Sin's correlate in its place — and constitutes the New Man with five virtues (love/faith/perfection/patience/wisdom). The closing draws an analogy: the great Mind shrinks within the body just as the gods/Watchers stand fixed but unmanifest in the cosmic Zone. The teaching's strict per-faculty parallelism and recurring formulae ('he raises X out of Y, binds Sin's X in Y'; 'just so also is this of the Mind of Light') tightly constrained most editor restorations, which I confirmed as high. I proposed moderate/low fills for short formulaic lacunae (e.g., ⲥⲱⲙⲁ at {78}, ⲥⲉϫⲉ at {58}, ⲡⲣⲙ̄ⲛ̄ⲃⲣ̄ⲣⲉ at {64}). The fragmentary middle (sections 2206-2213, where the soul is ignorant of her father) and several long lacunae (15-21 chars) lacked formulaic anchors and were left unrestorable.",
